WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.200
-Thank you for coming back.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.701
Last time, you came on the show
right before

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.000
"Black Panther:
Wakanda Forever."

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.501
-Yes.
-And I was like --

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:08.334
I had such a great time hanging
with you and talking with you.

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:09.634
-Yes.
-I'm like, "Let's have him back

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:11.667
after the movie comes out,"
just to see how you enjoy

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:13.467
being in one of the biggest...
-You missed me.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:14.834
You missed me.
-I really do.

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:17.000
I mean, look at you,
by the way. Now a cover boy.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.300
Oh, my gosh.
Look at this guy.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.634
-Oh, boy. Oh, boy.

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:23.133
-"The Winston Duke Era
Begins Now."

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:25.133
-Oh, the Winston Duke effect,
you know?

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:27.067
-Yes, the effect.
-I'll take it.

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:30.200
-Last time --
Last time you came on, you --

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.434
You're obviously
very good-looking and tall,

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:33.667
but you're also very --

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:34.901
-Continue.
You should do a couple more.

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.033
-Thank you. Yeah.

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:38.200
You're very strong,
and you actually --

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.634
You put me in a full Nelson
and almost killed me.

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:43.267
And people seemed to enjoy that.

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:46.567
But, tonight, you have
a new feat of strength

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:47.901
and a talent,
a different talent...

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.167
-Oh, boy.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:50.901
-...that you're gonna debut
involving an apple.

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:52.734
-Let's do it.
-Well, I mean, what --

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:55.167
First of all, how did you
figure out how to do this

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:56.467
and what are you going to do?

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.968
-You know, like
most hero origin stories...

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:01.400
[ Laughter ]
-My God.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:06.467
-Like most hero origin stories,
it came out of need.

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:08.067
-Yeah.
-Great need.

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.501
A friend of mine...
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:12.000
-...was really hungry
in grad school,

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.667
and I had an apple,
but only one.

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:16.367
One apple.
-Wow.

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:21.100
-And I decided I needed to
share this apple really badly.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.300
And somehow,
I summoned -- summoned!

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.767
-Wow.

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:28.934
-The strength to tear
this apple in half

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.734
so I could share it
with my friend,

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:32.968
a fellow actor
by the name of Mamoudou Athie.

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:34.167
-Wow.
-Yes.

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:36.400
-And so you did this --
-And I broke it.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.133
Well, first, the key.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.601
-Uh-huh.
-The key to the trick

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:48.234
is developing a bit
of a hand-hold space.

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:50.000
Right? So...

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.033
[ Crunch ]
Gentle bite.

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:54.467
-Wait. So you already
break the apple?

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:55.834
-Well, I was eating it.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:57.934
-Oh, oh, so, your friend --
so your --

00:01:57.934 --> 00:02:00.400
Oh, so your friend was --
-For the sake of accuracy,

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.334
I have to replicate the moment.

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:03.734
-Yes, I feel -- I feel you.

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:06.534
-So, I have a hand-hold.
-Oh, I see -- I understand.

00:02:06.534 --> 00:02:08.534
-'Cause I need --
I need a space for the fingers.

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:10.167
-Yes.

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:11.667
-Ahh.
-Wow!

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:13.701
Ladies and gentlemen.

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:16.267
Wait! Whoa!

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:17.467
Wait, wait. Stop. Stop!

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:18.801
-Ah.
-It's too much!

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:21.067
-I'm doing it for the Roots!
-It's too much strength!

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:23.334
It's too much strength!
-I'm doing it for the Roots!

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:25.901
-Look at this. This is
the best thing I've ever seen.

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:29.300
Look at this.
How beautiful that looks.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:30.734
Winston, this is a talent.

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:32.801
This is -- This is --
This doesn't end here.

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:35.567
This is going to go -- May I
have a piece of your apple?

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.801
-[ Laughs ] You can.
-Alright.

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:39.667
-That piece has no bite in it.
-Yeah.

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:41.100
Oh, it might have.
-It's still clean.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.634
-And I washed my hands
before I came out.

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:44.033
-Winston Duke,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:46.467
That's what
I'm talking about here.

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:50.100
-You never knew
a true superhero...

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.334
-Could break an apple
into a thousand pieces.

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:53.400
...could break in apple in half.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.000
Completely useless.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.501
Late time you were here, you
were promoting "Black Panther."

00:02:57.501 --> 00:02:59.534
We were talking about
what you're doing next.

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:00.834
You were going to the premiere.
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:02.133
-It didn't stop.

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:04.300
Have you had any time
to relax and enjoy yourself?

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.434
-Yeah, completely.
So, so much has changed,

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:09.834
you know, after doing
the Rihanna Fenty show.

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:11.434
-I mean, come on.

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:12.701
-You know? And --
-That's right!

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:14.801
-And having myself on the cover,
you know,

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:16.634
something that happened
that I didn't expect.

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:20.267
So all these big guys on Twitter

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:24.501
have now crowned me
the face of plus size,

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:26.701
of the plus-size movement.
-Is that right?

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:30.634
-I woke up one morning,
and I was plus size.

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:33.200
-It happens to --
It happens to a lot of people.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.367
-I had no idea.

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:35.801
-Happens to a lot of people.
-You know?

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:38.567
And I became the face
of the plus-size movement.

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:40.834
You know,
I've been sharing my apples,

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:42.868
and now I'm the face
of the plus-size movement.

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:44.167
-Yeah, well,
that must feel good, though.

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:45.434
-Yeah. It felt great.

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:49.634
And then I went to Mexico,
and I went for, like,

00:03:49.634 --> 00:03:52.100
a horseback ride,
like a little trail thing.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:56.133
And this horse had no idea
that I was the face of the --

00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:58.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.767 --> 00:03:59.968
the plus-size movement.

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:01.300
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-You know?

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.667
-No, he didn't know it at all.

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:04.534
-And this horse
was trying to play me, man.

00:04:04.534 --> 00:04:07.000
This horse...
-He did not enjoy --

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.667
-...didn't want me on his back.

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:10.501
This horse
was throwing tantrums.

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:13.501
It was like --
[ Mimicking horse noises ]

00:04:13.501 --> 00:04:14.701
-It looked back at you?

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:18.067
-It looked back at me,
exasperated.

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:20.234
-The guy's like,
"No, just, like, kick him,

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:22.167
and, like, he's just lazy.
He's lazy."

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:27.067
We got to a mild incline --
a mild incline.

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:29.133
And the horse stopped,

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:32.033
looked at me,
looked back at the incline,

00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:33.634
and decided
it was not gonna go.

00:04:33.634 --> 00:04:36.667
-Yeah. "Get off. Get off."

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:39.634
-The horse -- I was trying to --
Everyone was leaving me behind.

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:42.634
So I'm, like, trying to go fast.

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:44.033
We're finally getting back

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:45.801
after maybe like two hours
on this horse.

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.868
-Yeah.
-The horse finally sees home.

00:04:47.868 --> 00:04:51.234
And that's the first time on
that trip that the horse ran.

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:53.367
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah!

00:04:53.367 --> 00:04:54.901
-The horse ran with, like --

00:04:54.901 --> 00:04:57.367
With, like, maybe 20 feet left,
it sprinted.

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:58.868
I got off the horse.

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:01.834
And the horse literally
just started, like, shaking...

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.100
-You go, "Who are you?"

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:06.567
-It stopped, it turned around,
it looked at me...

00:05:06.567 --> 00:05:07.801
-And said...

00:05:07.801 --> 00:05:10.334
-...and just was like,
"You should know better."

00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:12.601
And then walked in.
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:05:12.601 --> 00:05:14.634
-Walked away. It left.
You never saw the horse again.

00:05:14.634 --> 00:05:17.000
-So this horse has no respect
for the thick thigh nation.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.767
-Yeah, no, but --

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:20.701
-You know what I'm saying?
-Thick thigh nation.

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:22.567
-For thick thigh nation.
-He didn't know who he had on --

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:24.634
-Has no idea
that I'm the ambassador.

00:05:24.634 --> 00:05:26.000
-Yes, you really are.
-You know?

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.701
-But now, I mean, look,
the movie

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:28.968
was not only number one.

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:30.534
It was number one for,
like, five weeks in a row.

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:33.200
-Five weeks, yes.
-I mean, you couldn't get a --

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.701
-It's also the top grossing

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:38.300
female-led superhero film
in the country.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:43.234
-And also --
can I just say, too,

00:05:43.234 --> 00:05:44.934
after watching it, I loved it

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:46.434
and I thought
you were fantastic in it.

00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:50.400
But, also, it's unlike
any Marvel movie in a way.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.400
because I felt --
I felt like this one

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.534
was more emotional
than any of them have been.

00:05:54.534 --> 00:05:55.868
-Yeah, you know, the first one

00:05:55.868 --> 00:05:57.467
really caught everyone
off guard.

00:05:57.467 --> 00:06:00.234
The first one,
no one knew what to expect.

00:06:00.234 --> 00:06:02.400
And it became this beautiful
watershed moment

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:04.567
for everyone to kind of
recognize themselves.

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:06.033
And then it, you know,

00:06:06.033 --> 00:06:09.133
of course, it would be
something hard to follow up.

00:06:09.133 --> 00:06:12.300
And then we lost Chadwick,
and, you know,

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.434
the circumstance
became what it was.

00:06:14.434 --> 00:06:18.067
And it became this opportunity
for us all to kind of come

00:06:18.067 --> 00:06:20.501
to grips with the grief
that we've all been feeling.

00:06:20.501 --> 00:06:22.367
-Yeah.
-And it became this opportunity

00:06:22.367 --> 00:06:24.300
to say goodbye to Chadwick

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.834
and to give ourselves permission
to grieve.

00:06:26.834 --> 00:06:28.367
The movie is about grief.

00:06:28.367 --> 00:06:30.901
The movie is about, there's no
such thing as the right time.

00:06:30.901 --> 00:06:33.367
There's no such thing
as the right way to grieve.

00:06:33.367 --> 00:06:36.534
And the only way to do it
is to get through it.

00:06:36.534 --> 00:06:39.267
And people really got a chance
to do that with the film.

00:06:39.267 --> 00:06:41.067
So, it became
so much more -- again --

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:42.934
'Cause that was the thing.
It was like,

00:06:42.934 --> 00:06:45.434
"How do we create something,

00:06:45.434 --> 00:06:48.267
and not feel like we're trying
to replicate the first movie?"

00:06:48.267 --> 00:06:51.601
-Yeah.
-And we found a way into it

00:06:51.601 --> 00:06:54.467
by just embracing the truth
of the moment that we were in.

00:06:54.467 --> 00:06:57.000
-That's what I'm talking about.
Bud, I'm so happy for you.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.300
It couldn't happen to a nicer
guy. Congratulations.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.501
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Winston Duke

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:03.601
in "Black Panther:
Wakanda Forever."

00:07:03.601 --> 00:07:04.934
Take a look at this.

00:07:04.934 --> 00:07:07.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:07.701 --> 00:07:12.834
-The river border
has been breached, huh?

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:14.601
If my soldiers were present,

00:07:14.601 --> 00:07:18.634
this fish-man would be bound
before us as we speak.

00:07:18.634 --> 00:07:21.334
-If your muscle brains
were present,

00:07:21.334 --> 00:07:22.968
they would still be there

00:07:22.968 --> 00:07:24.467
choking on their
fuzzy adornments.

00:07:24.467 --> 00:07:27.934
-You bald-headed demon.
-Show some respect, you two.

00:07:27.934 --> 00:07:31.467
-Respect? These men should be
ashamed to show their faces!

00:07:31.467 --> 00:07:32.968
-Watch your tone, Jabari.

00:07:32.968 --> 00:07:36.801
[ Affronted chanting ]

00:07:36.801 --> 00:07:38.234
-Hey!

00:07:38.234 --> 00:07:42.701
[ Spears clanking ]

00:07:42.701 --> 00:07:44.000
[ Crunch ]

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:46.167
-Yeah!
That's what I'm talking about.

00:07:46.167 --> 00:07:50.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:50.968 --> 00:07:53.734
Before -- Before you go,

00:07:53.734 --> 00:07:57.234
I was wondering if you could
teach us the Jabari chant.

00:07:57.234 --> 00:07:59.701
-Oh, man. Do you guys
want to learn the chant?

00:07:59.701 --> 00:08:01.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I mean --

00:08:01.801 --> 00:08:03.000
Come on. Only you --

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.067
-Okay. Alright.
-Only you. The one and only.

00:08:05.067 --> 00:08:06.601
Ohh!

00:08:06.601 --> 00:08:08.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:08.133 --> 00:08:10.801
Wow! Okay.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:08:10.801 --> 00:08:11.968
Alright.

00:08:11.968 --> 00:08:13.334
-We like giving the people
what they want.

00:08:13.334 --> 00:08:15.133
-Yes, you have to give the
people what they want. Okay.

00:08:15.133 --> 00:08:18.868
-So, when I say "meri ha"...
-Yes!

00:08:18.868 --> 00:08:23.267
-That's a word that translates
to "win them."

00:08:23.267 --> 00:08:25.601
-Yeah.
-You're going to say, "Ya."

00:08:25.601 --> 00:08:27.868
I'm gonna grunt. Right?

00:08:27.868 --> 00:08:30.801
That's the --
The gorilla tribe's grunt.

00:08:30.801 --> 00:08:33.133
"Ooh."
You just repeat "ooh."

00:08:33.133 --> 00:08:34.701
So, I say, "Meri ha,"
you say, "Ya."

00:08:34.701 --> 00:08:35.868
-Ya.

00:08:35.868 --> 00:08:38.033
-I say, "ooh."
-Audience: Ooh.

00:08:38.033 --> 00:08:39.734
-Meri ha!
-Audience: Ya!

00:08:39.734 --> 00:08:40.934
-Ooh!
-Audience: Ooh!

00:08:40.934 --> 00:08:42.167
-Meri ha!
-Audience: Ya!

00:08:42.167 --> 00:08:43.300
-Ooh!
-Audience: Ooh!

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:46.734
[ Repeated chanting ]

00:08:46.734 --> 00:08:48.634
[ Drum beating ]

00:08:48.634 --> 00:08:54.501
[ Repeated chanting ]

00:08:54.501 --> 00:09:00.434
[ Repeated chanting ]

00:09:00.434 --> 00:09:02.167
-Winston Duke, everybody!

00:09:02.167 --> 00:09:04.100
"Black Panther:
Wakanda Forever"

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.601
comes to Disney Plus
February 1st.

00:09:06.601 --> 00:09:08.567
Available on DVD
and Blu-Ray soon.

00:09:08.567 --> 00:09:10.634
We'll be right back
with more "Tonight Show."

